#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183862 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af228cc4-8be2-5c16-8537-4e5dab4e2ff4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Horizontal Stretch and Vertical Shift of a Transformed Tangent Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "0431c02c-9a72-5d5b-ad75-550f413b74f1" :question/math-academy-id "e-10025" :question/problem "The graph above shows the function $y = \\tan(Bx) + D$, where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B + D$?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3850/Source/Images/eb20bf9f9c01a9caff32aae31f5d3d3c.png)" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT = \\dfrac{\\pi}{5} - \\left(-\\dfrac{\\pi}{5}\\right) = \\dfrac{2\\pi}{5}\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function\n\n$$\ny = A\\tan(Bx + C) + D\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\nT = \\dfrac{\\pi}{B}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2\\pi}{5} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{B} \\quad\\Longrightarrow \\quad B = \\dfrac{\\pi}{\\left(\\dfrac{2\\pi}{5}\\right)} = \\dfrac{5}{2}\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. The graph shows that the function has been translated by $1$ unit up. Hence, $D = 1$.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nB + D =\\dfrac{5}{2} +1 = \\dfrac{7}{2}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny = \\tan\\left(\\frac{5x}{2} \\right) +1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183999 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dac9c72b-c23f-56fa-b939-6e3b56d3a13b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Horizontal Stretch and Vertical Shift of a Transformed Cotangent Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "fdd0c8ab-6977-5a8f-b1db-37ae9b2b116e" :question/math-academy-id "e-3663" :question/problem "The graph below shows the function $y=\\cot{(Bx)}+D$, where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What are the values of $B$ and $D$?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3850/Source/Images/a5320a03808d49301adbe9c8f8dd0122.png)" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac \\pi 2\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function\n\n$$\ny=A\\cot(Bx + C) + D\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\nT = \\dfrac{\\pi}{B}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac \\pi 2 = \\dfrac{\\pi}{B}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad B = \\dfrac{\\pi}{\\left(\\dfrac \\pi 2\\right)} = 2\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $1$ unit down. Therefore, $D=-1$.\n\nSo, the final equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\cot\\left(2x\\right)-1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184000 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84355770-5926-5be6-9b9f-c13bb05599ae" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Horizontal Shift of a Horizontally Stretched Tangent or Cotangent Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "90986bdd-15dd-51c6-b5b0-4174542736c9" :question/math-academy-id "e-3669" :question/problem "The graph above shows the function $y=\\tan{\\left(2x+C\\right)}$, where $C$ is a constant. Given that $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{2} < C < \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$, what is the value of $C$?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3850/Source/Images/9ca2e643947437ad9a25d7a152252f4b.png)" :question/worked-solution "The parameter $C$ represents a horizontal shift of the function.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the function by factoring the horizontal stretch factor, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= \\tan (2x + C) \\\\\n&= \\tan (2(x + \\frac{C}{2}))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that our curve has been obtained by shifting $y=\\tan 2x$ by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\n$$\n\nunits to the right. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{C}{2} = -\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad C = -\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184769 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af228cc4-8be2-5c16-8537-4e5dab4e2ff4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Horizontal Stretch and Vertical Shift of a Transformed Tangent Curve"}] :questi